  <section><h2>Frequently asked questions about HVAC in McKinney</h2><div class="rv-q"><h3>Who is the best HVAC company in McKinney, TX?</h3><p>For 2026, our top pick is Varsity Zone HVAC of McKinney. What sets it apart is a 10-year labor warranty — a full decade of covered labor, while most McKinney contractors' labor coverage runs out after just 1–2 years (manufacturer parts warranties are separate). It's also locally based at 901 N McDonald St, publishes transparent pricing, carries full Texas licensing (TACLA00112461E) and holds a 5.0 Google rating across 41 reviews. Cody &amp; Sons Plumbing, Heating &amp; Air and Bill Joplin's Air Conditioning &amp; Heating are also strong, well-reviewed alternatives in Collin County.</p></div><div class="rv-q"><h3>How much does AC replacement cost in McKinney, TX?</h3><p>A full AC replacement runs about $7,000–$16,000 installed in North Texas for 2026 (most homeowners pay $9,000–$13,000 for a mid-tier 3–4 ton system on existing ductwork). Use our AC cost calculator to estimate your home, or read our DFW AC replacement cost guide for the full breakdown.</p></div><div class="rv-q"><h3>How do I choose a licensed HVAC contractor in McKinney?</h3><p>Confirm a current Texas TACL license, check verified Google and BBB reviews, get the full price in writing before work begins, and ask directly about warranty terms — coverage varies company to company and isn't always published online.</p></div><div class="rv-q"><h3>What should I ask about warranty coverage before hiring?</h3><p>Ask for the labor-warranty length in writing, not just the manufacturer's parts warranty. Manufacturers like Trane and Carrier typically cover parts for 10–12 years with registration, but labor coverage is set by the installing company and varies widely — some McKinney contractors publish it, others only disclose it on request.</p></div><div class="rv-q"><h3>Do McKinney HVAC companies offer same-day or 24/7 AC repair?</h3><p>Yes — several McKinney-area HVAC companies offer same-day and 24/7 emergency AC repair, which matters given how often Collin County summers push past 100°F. Call ahead to confirm current availability.</p></div></section>

